  {
    "sha": "49904407ffcb4079942c4592ef5a9f0dca4224b2",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVoU8JdoAKDQ5OTA0NDA3ZmZjYjQwNzk5NDJjNDU5MmVmNWE5ZjBkY2E0MjI0YjI",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-12T10:08:21Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-12T10:08:21Z"
      },
      "message": "feat(edm): sinker orbit patterns (circular, vector, planetary) as explicit moves\n\nA Sinker Burn can now orbit at the burn floor. After the plunge, the\nelectrode's circular, vector or planetary excursion is expanded into\nexplicit Feed chords (#290 D3), so the 3-axis stock sim's box atom\nverifies every move that posts, corner joins included. Every vertex\nlies on or inside the stated radius, so no move overshoots it. The\ncircle's vertices include the four axis directions, so a rectangular\nelectrode's cavity widens by exactly the radius.\n\nThe pattern must be one the setup's sinker lists under edm.orbits, and\nthe radius must be within its stated edm.max_orbit_radius (#290 D6).\nBoth fields come from the #530 schema and are unchanged here. Each is\nrefused by name at generation, and an unstated maximum is refused\nrather than read as unlimited. The orbit is an additive op field and\nfile key, so a plain plunge keeps its CL and digest. MCP reaches it\nthrough the params JSON door. No new command.\n\nPinned by tests/sinker_orbit.rs (golden sinker_orbit_circular.cl) and\nmotion::sinker_orbit unit tests. Not exercised on a real EDM control.\n\nFixes #544\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
